From cdb3415dc6f6d0db46de0192aeb41eb68d3fe880 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:20:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/27] Typer: sigrounds (signatures of extensions and givens
 computed in rounds), assocsubst (instantiate associated types of generic
 conformances)

sigrounds computes the signatures of all extensions, conformances and given
bindings of a module before checking it, in rounds that each start from the
pristine typing state and read the signatures of the previous round only, until
the table is stable. The result no longer depends on the order of declarations.

assocsubst substitutes the type arguments of a witness into the associated type
read from a generic conformance, so that Box<A>.X and Box<C>.X are distinct.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
